# iso/packages.x86_64 — live-env packages for the netinstall ISO.
# MINIMAL on purpose: just enough to fetch the repo and run archinstall.
# Everything in config/packages is installed into the TARGET later.
# NOTE: linux (kernel) is mandatory here — mkarchiso builds the ISO boot
# images from it. mkinitcpio-archiso provides the live-boot hooks; without
# it the ISO drops to emergency mode (gpt-auto-root timeout).
linux
mkinitcpio-archiso
systemd-sysvcompat
archlinux-keyring
# ^ provides the wkd-sync timer+service archinstall waits on. Without it
# the install hangs forever at keyring sync with no process to blame.
# ^ provides /usr/bin/{init,halt,reboot,poweroff,shutdown}. Without it the
# live env mounts root then bails (/sbin/init missing). Also silences the
# invalid-symlink noise at initramfs build time. (Verified Sep 2026.)
archinstall
git
python
sudo
nano
vim
openssh
# ^ sshd for host->guest access (slirp hostfwd); not needed by installer.
syslinux
networkmanager
iwd
wireless_tools
wpa_supplicant
smartmontools
usbutils
iputils
pciutils
reflector
# ^ refreshes the live mirrorlist on boot (official-ISO behavior).
# Without it the live env inherits a stale all-commented mirrorlist
# (pacman: no servers configured).
efibootmgr
dosfstools
btrfs-progs
openssl
curl
